  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1155 PM CDT SAT SEP 26 2026\n\nThis evening, surface ridging is in place across Eastern Conus.\nIn the upper levels, a ridge is present across Mexico with a\nlarge low just off of the Mid Atlantic Coast resulting in\nnorthwest flow into Alabama. In the short term, look for pleasant\ntemperatures along with low humidity and rain free conditions.\nThere will be some weak disturbances through the upper flow\naround the trough, but lower moisture will be quite limited with\nonly some mid/upper clouds expected. By the middle of the upcoming\nweek, a boundary is expected to move back northward as a warm front\nbefore fizzling out yielding increased moisture across Central \nAlabama with overall south to southeast onshore flow. At the same \ntime, the upper ridge over Mexico will get infringed upon by a low\nmoving eastward out of California into New Mexico with weak flow \nover Alabama. Toward the latter half of the week, guidance shows \ntemperatures moderating upward with our return to a warmer onshore\nflow. Moisture will need to recover a bit before we can expect \nany significant rain chances. Low rain chances return by Thursday \nfor portions of the area. However, more substantial chances hold \noff until next weekend ahead of an approaching front.\n\n08",
